### Step 1: Total Area of the Grid
The grid is a 5x5 matrix of small squares, each measuring 2 cm by 2 cm. The area of one small square is:
\[ 2 \, \text{cm} \times 2 \, \text{cm} = 4 \, \text{cm}^2 \]
With 25 small squares, the total area of the grid is:
\[ 25 \times 4 \, \text{cm}^2 = 100 \, \text{cm}^2 \]

