  There are 4 small circles, so their total area is:
  \[ 4 \times \pi \, \text{cm}^2 = 4\pi \, \text{cm}^2 \]

- **Large Circle**: It has a radius of 1.5 Asymptote units. Converting to cm: \(1.5 \times 2 = 3 \, \text{cm}\). The area of the large circle is:
